cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: robustmargin
authors:
  - family-names: Badkoubeh
    given-names: Babak
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3586-7901"
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/robustmargin/robustmargin"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/robustmargin/"
abstract: >-
  robustmargin estimates robustness margins with confidence intervals via
  dose-response threshold estimation. It fits binomial generalised linear
  models with probit, logit or complementary log-log links to success counts
  observed at increasing severity levels, and reports the severity at which
  performance crosses a chosen level, with profile-likelihood or delta-method
  intervals. When the data cannot support an estimate, a threshold beyond the
  tested range is reported as an exact censoring bound and a failed fit is
  flagged rather than given a number. It is domain-neutral and needs no GPU or
  machine-learning framework.
keywords:
  - dose-response
  - threshold estimation
  - robustness margin
  - confidence intervals
  - binomial regression
  - statistics
